        {
          "url": "https://teaching.cornell.edu/teaching-resources/assessment-evaluation/measuring-student-learning",
          "section": "Best Practices for Assessing Student Learning",
          "retrievedAt": "2026-10-12T22:46:39Z",
          "textSha256": "7ea119f23d8dac6bce6289764698fc48f31274561b8fa03ae553eb7f891831e7"
        }
      ],
      "recommendation": "Either narrow o2 and the cumulative-review wording to the workflow actually checked, or—without adding syllabus—replace/extend the review checks with a compact mixed retrieval set sampling the already-taught undo, stash, remote, conflict, merge/rebase and PR decisions. Keep the seven-minute budget by prioritizing retrieval over recap repetition.",
